  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Over two sweltering, bug-swarming weeks in July [July 10-21, 2014], the LBM Dispatch crew (superbly assisted by Stephen Milner and Brett Schenning) covered 2,400 miles in Georgia, exploring the State's diverse landscapes, histories, and narratives that were alternately harrowing and inspiring. From the Civil War to the last beleaguered Gullah Geechee community on Sapelo Island, the result is a sort of see-sawing time-lapse portrait of a region that continues to straddle the past and the present, and that seems to exist in a state of conflicted nostalgia and perpetual reconstruction. The LBM Dispatch is an irregularly published newspaper of the North American ramblings of photographer Alec Soth and writer Brad Zellar"--Publisher's Web site, viewed December 11, 2014.</subfield>
  </datafield>
